WEBVTT

00:12.012 --> 00:14.097
Give me four days
and I can arrange the flight.

00:17.976 --> 00:19.352
So, where are we going?

00:19.436 --> 00:21.563
I'm thinking maybe Thailand or Vietnam,

00:21.646 --> 00:25.066
but it might be easier for you in Thailand
because you know people there.

00:25.150 --> 00:25.984
Yeah.

00:27.652 --> 00:29.738
I'll go through and make the arrangements.

00:29.821 --> 00:33.742
I'd also recommend
some S-class bloodhounds.

00:34.409 --> 00:36.536
If you have three,
then that should get the job done.

00:36.619 --> 00:37.954
That is

00:38.538 --> 00:41.166
if you're trying
to kidnap Kim Gun-woo's mother.

00:41.833 --> 00:42.834
How much?

00:42.917 --> 00:45.795
300 million each. So 900 million.

00:47.964 --> 00:50.091
You're wanted and we don't have much time.

00:50.175 --> 00:52.052
We have to do this the right way.

00:52.135 --> 00:53.428
It's a

00:54.554 --> 00:55.847
necessary investment.

00:56.514 --> 00:58.224
S-class is special,

00:58.892 --> 01:01.144
I promise you with my life,

01:02.479 --> 01:05.482
because they'll do the job right.

01:08.359 --> 01:11.154
Get us two, would ya? You're number three.

01:14.991 --> 01:15.909
I understand.

01:18.078 --> 01:19.579
Who's that?

01:20.747 --> 01:21.790
It's just my mother.

01:22.540 --> 01:23.374
Then take it.

01:26.753 --> 01:28.671
-Hey.
-Where are you right now?

01:28.755 --> 01:30.757
-Why?
-Min-a got hit by a car.

01:30.840 --> 01:32.842
What? How bad is it?

01:33.510 --> 01:36.179
-Where are you?
-The ER at Seonkuk University Medical.

01:36.262 --> 01:38.723
-Hurry up and get here.
-Got it.

01:42.727 --> 01:45.396
My daughter was hit by a car.
They're at the hospital.

01:53.321 --> 01:54.280
Go then.

02:25.395 --> 02:26.855
Show me your ID, please.

02:28.022 --> 02:30.441
Just a second.

02:31.484 --> 02:33.570
-And the name of the patient?
-Yun Min-a.

02:33.653 --> 02:36.656
Okay, come on in.
Room's around the corner and to the left.

02:45.290 --> 02:46.124
Min-a.

02:47.208 --> 02:48.501
Oh, Dad!

02:49.127 --> 02:50.712
I need you all in position.

02:55.884 --> 02:56.718
Are you okay?

02:57.302 --> 02:58.219
Huh?

03:00.972 --> 03:02.557
Listen to me.

03:03.057 --> 03:05.351
Please stop doing this.

03:08.396 --> 03:09.814
Tae-geom. Tae-geom!

03:11.566 --> 03:12.734
That's enough. Hey, stop!

03:14.152 --> 03:16.321
Hey, hey, hey, hey. Put the guns down.

03:16.404 --> 03:18.031
-Put the guns down.
-Min-a.

03:19.073 --> 03:20.700
Close your eyes and hold on tight.

03:21.451 --> 03:23.077
It's all right. Put them down.

03:28.917 --> 03:31.252
Hey! Put them down. It's okay.

03:32.712 --> 03:33.630
It's okay.

03:38.760 --> 03:40.053
Tae-geom, hey.

03:40.762 --> 03:41.930
We're not gonna hurt you.

03:44.557 --> 03:45.600
Let's just talk.

03:46.601 --> 03:49.229
I promise, I'm really just here
to talk to you.

03:55.860 --> 03:58.947
I also have a young daughter.

04:01.741 --> 04:03.201
From one dad to another,

04:04.035 --> 04:05.495
let's just talk about it.

04:23.304 --> 04:24.639
Sir, what brings you in?

04:29.978 --> 04:32.480
A guest sent by your uncle
has arrived, sir.

04:42.490 --> 04:44.659
I want to thank you for coming here.

04:52.583 --> 04:54.377
Nice to meet you. I'm Choi Sin-hyeong.

04:57.255 --> 04:59.841
Hmm. I know the name's a bit unusual.

05:00.842 --> 05:02.385
It's a code name I go by.

05:33.291 --> 05:35.835
BLOODHOUNDS 2

05:39.756 --> 05:43.426
If they were to bring you in, you'd get
a life sentence or the death penalty.

05:43.509 --> 05:46.929
If you help us, I'll do my very best
to get you the life sentence.

05:47.013 --> 05:49.474
And what would be the point of that?

05:49.557 --> 05:53.811
If you're sentenced to death, you won't
be able to have visitors or seek parole.

05:53.895 --> 05:56.814
But with a life sentence,
it could be possible to get parole,

05:57.315 --> 05:58.566
assuming that you're good.

06:05.907 --> 06:07.241
Yun Tae-geom, sir.

06:08.701 --> 06:10.036
I mean, bro.

06:11.621 --> 06:15.375
Didn't you start working under
Im Baek-jeong to provide for your family?

06:16.376 --> 06:19.462
Well, then, you should do
whatever it takes

06:19.545 --> 06:21.881
so you can live
to protect your mother and daughter.

06:22.507 --> 06:26.803
Your family? They're never gonna give up
on you, no matter how much you screw up.

06:26.886 --> 06:28.221
And your mother?

06:28.721 --> 06:31.933
That woman would do almost anything
to save her child, even if it kills her.

06:32.016 --> 06:33.935
You know that. And your daughter?

06:34.435 --> 06:39.941
Hey, man, your daughter, I bet she'd wait
her whole fucking life just to see you.

06:40.566 --> 06:43.820
But man, "the point?"

06:44.320 --> 06:47.198
You can't see the point? Is that it, huh?

06:47.698 --> 06:49.700
Is that the type of dad that they need?

06:50.868 --> 06:51.702
Fine, then.

06:52.412 --> 06:53.454
Be that guy.

06:57.083 --> 06:57.917
Tae-geom, please.

06:59.460 --> 07:01.421
It's not over until it's over.

07:02.296 --> 07:05.049
We could still do more for each other.
I'm sure of it.

07:07.844 --> 07:09.262
So, how about you join us?

07:18.938 --> 07:21.649
Keep my family safe from Im Baek-jeong.

07:24.152 --> 07:25.445
I promise you that.

07:29.907 --> 07:31.033
What do you want me to say?

07:32.326 --> 07:34.954
Well, first, where is Im Baek-jeong?

07:35.455 --> 07:37.665
He's on the move,
aboard his yacht on the Han River.

07:38.749 --> 07:40.626
If I contact him,
he'll tell me the pickup point.

07:40.710 --> 07:43.504
The yacht could be docking
at one of three positions.

07:45.131 --> 07:46.507
He's a smart guy.

07:49.135 --> 07:50.511
How about we raid them tonight?

07:50.595 --> 07:52.805
If by chance we fail to arrest him,

07:52.889 --> 07:54.974
won't Tae-geom be in danger?

07:55.558 --> 07:58.227
How about we maintain his cover
and wait for the right opportunity?

07:59.395 --> 08:01.606
We could. You're right.

08:03.316 --> 08:06.861
But, um, how did he know
we would be raiding the Entra Hotel?

08:06.944 --> 08:09.280
I believe he was informed by an employee.

08:11.032 --> 08:12.575
Lots of people in his circle, then?

08:12.658 --> 08:13.743
Yes.

08:14.243 --> 08:16.746
Who's organizing all this for him?
That's what I need from you.

08:16.829 --> 08:19.290
Could it… could it be a cop?

08:19.373 --> 08:22.502
There's a guy called Lee Dong-hyeon.
He was an NIS agent.

08:25.713 --> 08:26.797
Lee Man-bae, right?

08:27.381 --> 08:28.966
His actual name is Lee Dong-hyeon.

08:29.050 --> 08:31.844
Is he the one
who gave the order to kill Gi-na?

08:31.928 --> 08:32.887
Yes.

08:33.387 --> 08:35.097
So, who in the police force
does he control?

08:35.181 --> 08:36.807
I'm not sure yet.

08:37.850 --> 08:39.644
I know for sure there was more than one.

08:39.727 --> 08:41.646
I could hear that much
from his phone call.

08:42.230 --> 08:43.773
He's a meticulous man.

08:44.440 --> 08:46.901
Then it's possible he could have heard
about the wanted alert.

08:48.152 --> 08:50.363
Lee Dong-hyeon's looking
for a private plane.

08:50.863 --> 08:52.323
I'll bet you he's going to Thailand.

08:54.242 --> 08:56.160
He couldn't do that with a warrant though.

08:56.244 --> 08:58.621
He's the kind of man
that would make it happen.

09:01.332 --> 09:02.583
Our goal

09:03.960 --> 09:06.963
is to capture Kim Gun-woo's mother
and take her to Thailand.

09:07.046 --> 09:09.465
Im Baek-jeong wants
to fight Kim Gun-woo again.

09:10.299 --> 09:12.426
So he plans to kidnap his mother
to lure him in.

09:12.510 --> 09:13.719
For ransom money?

09:14.637 --> 09:17.848
It seems that Baek-jeong
has a more personal reason.

09:18.683 --> 09:22.144
I think he believes he lost to Kim Gun-woo
in that previous fight they had.

09:23.854 --> 09:27.275
Because viewers all over the world
rooted for Kim Gun-woo to win.

09:28.734 --> 09:30.361
So while everyone's watching,

09:32.238 --> 09:33.739
Kim Gun-woo's going to be killed.

09:35.283 --> 09:36.993
Gun-woo's gonna what?

09:39.287 --> 09:41.914
There are a few ways to fight in the IKFC.

09:41.998 --> 09:44.041
One of those is a death match.

09:44.875 --> 09:46.586
They fight until one of them dies.

09:47.295 --> 09:49.380
That's the fight
that makes the most money.

09:49.463 --> 09:52.425
So kidnapping Gun-woo's mother.
How's he doing it?

09:52.508 --> 09:54.677
Dong-hyeon is paying S-class bloodhounds.

09:54.760 --> 09:55.636
What's that?

09:56.804 --> 09:59.015
They're professional killers for hire.

09:59.098 --> 10:03.936
The S-class means that Dong-hyeon's people
are as deadly as they could be.

10:04.520 --> 10:08.107
So then, do you think he also knows
where Gun-woo's mother is staying?

10:09.650 --> 10:10.568
I don't have a clue.

10:10.651 --> 10:12.194
It wasn't ever mentioned?

10:14.071 --> 10:15.072
No.

10:19.035 --> 10:20.494
PRESIDENT

10:21.370 --> 10:22.204
Im Baek-jeong?

10:24.290 --> 10:28.294
Let's tell him that Min-a hurt her head
and she's waiting for a scan right now.

10:33.633 --> 10:34.800
Sir.

10:34.884 --> 10:36.010
How is she?

10:36.093 --> 10:39.639
She hit her head pretty bad on the ground.
She's gonna get a CT scan.

10:45.811 --> 10:48.356
-Wrap it up and get back.
-Okay.

10:51.442 --> 10:52.443
Tae-geom.

11:04.664 --> 11:06.707
-Kim Jin-su, please come in.
-Okay.

11:10.336 --> 11:13.464
The wound is healing well,
so you don't have anything to worry about.

11:13.547 --> 11:14.632
I appreciate it.

11:20.137 --> 11:21.263
How's your shoulder?

11:21.347 --> 11:23.891
Um, it hurts a little.

11:24.392 --> 11:25.476
Could I see it?

11:32.149 --> 11:33.442
Do you need painkillers?

11:35.027 --> 11:36.028
I'll be okay.

11:36.862 --> 11:37.905
All right, then.

11:51.794 --> 11:52.670
Min-beom.

11:56.048 --> 11:57.383
How's it going?

11:58.592 --> 12:00.177
This room is so small.

12:00.803 --> 12:02.179
You want me to upgrade you?

12:03.013 --> 12:06.100
Oh, no, this room's already
too much for me, but thanks anyway.

12:06.684 --> 12:08.561
I'm going to the hospital
to visit Gang-yong.

12:08.644 --> 12:11.522
-Could you let me come?
-No, you shouldn't.

12:12.732 --> 12:14.233
I'll talk to him and call you.

12:16.736 --> 12:17.945
Just rest up.

12:18.654 --> 12:19.530
Okay.

12:38.966 --> 12:40.968
Seul-gi, have you thought
about your code name?

12:41.552 --> 12:42.887
I haven't thought of anything yet.

12:44.054 --> 12:45.973
You know, your look is delicate,

12:46.056 --> 12:48.726
so it's important
that you pick a strong name.

12:49.393 --> 12:52.313
Something like… Jung Hwa-gi.

12:54.231 --> 12:55.149
Jung Hwa-gi?

12:59.862 --> 13:02.323
-You don't like it?
-It'd be an honor.

13:05.367 --> 13:06.285
I'm just joking.

13:06.368 --> 13:08.829
What kind of name is Hwa-gi?

13:12.041 --> 13:13.209
How about Kang Ryeok-han?

13:16.086 --> 13:17.004
Ryeok-han?

13:19.006 --> 13:19.840
Mm.

13:23.761 --> 13:24.762
Incredible.

13:26.388 --> 13:28.766
I'm good at making code names.

13:36.106 --> 13:36.941
Hello?

13:37.525 --> 13:39.610
-The meeting's about to start.
-All right.

13:42.696 --> 13:45.241
HONG MIN-BEOM
PRESIDENT OF IIL GROUP

13:45.324 --> 13:48.953
We'll have two chances.
When they come to kidnap Gun-woo's mother.

13:49.453 --> 13:51.539
And when they get off the yacht
to flee abroad.

13:52.957 --> 13:54.959
Is this person trustworthy?

13:55.042 --> 13:56.377
Yun Tae-geom?

13:57.336 --> 14:00.714
-We'd say he's worthy of your trust.
-Hmm. I agree with that.

14:01.382 --> 14:04.093
How about Gun-woo's mother? Is she safe?

14:04.176 --> 14:06.220
Well, we did talk about that too.

14:06.303 --> 14:08.138
Where she's at now is the safest.

14:08.222 --> 14:10.266
Woo-jin and Woo-jeong
will stay at the hotel

14:10.349 --> 14:11.934
and they have guards to keep her safe.

14:12.935 --> 14:14.728
So if they're after his mother,

14:15.980 --> 14:17.106
does Gun-woo know?

14:17.731 --> 14:20.985
He doesn't know. Gun-woo wouldn't
think twice about leaving the hospital.

14:21.652 --> 14:22.862
Probably, yeah.

14:24.572 --> 14:28.158
I'd like it if he could just focus
on his recovery.

14:28.868 --> 14:31.287
I believe we can ensure
his mother's safety.

14:31.829 --> 14:34.874
It'll be more dangerous
if Gun-woo fights in his current state.

14:38.168 --> 14:39.211
So…

14:41.255 --> 14:43.090
what do we do once we catch 'em?

14:43.924 --> 14:44.800
Hmm?

14:50.723 --> 14:52.349
Punish them to the fullest legal extent.

14:54.351 --> 14:56.186
That doesn't feel like enough.

14:56.270 --> 14:58.647
I'm still anxious
with Kim Myeong-gil behind bars.

14:58.731 --> 15:00.649
We need something… more.

15:02.568 --> 15:04.320
So then how do you wanna deal with it?

15:06.363 --> 15:07.823
Could you excuse us?

15:08.324 --> 15:09.909
No, Gwang-mu, it's okay.

15:11.577 --> 15:12.953
It's okay. Just say it.

15:21.337 --> 15:22.296
I want him dead.

15:25.799 --> 15:26.800
My uncle

15:27.509 --> 15:29.136
assigned some agents to me.

15:31.639 --> 15:32.890
What kind of agents?

15:33.891 --> 15:34.850
Black ops.

15:36.894 --> 15:40.856
This issue is ours. There's
no reason for the NIS to get involved.

15:40.940 --> 15:43.651
-Well, can you kill these guys?
-Min-beom.

15:44.276 --> 15:48.364
We have to… let them
spend the rest of their lives in jail,

15:48.447 --> 15:49.698
reflecting on what they've done,

15:49.782 --> 15:52.701
and return all that stolen wealth
back to society.

15:53.285 --> 15:54.161
Do you understand?

15:58.624 --> 16:01.126
I need to see these stupid fucks gone.

16:02.461 --> 16:03.629
You know that isn't justice.

16:03.712 --> 16:05.381
I have people.

16:05.464 --> 16:08.509
Min-beom, we need to be
on the same page about this.

16:14.556 --> 16:16.016
Then I'll do it my way.

16:29.655 --> 16:32.616
You should know, my dad won bronze
at the Barcelona Olympics,

16:33.784 --> 16:38.080
so I asked him if he happened
to know of a guy named Im Baek-jeong.

16:39.456 --> 16:41.917
Apparently, Im Baek-jeong
was a student to his friend.

16:42.668 --> 16:43.711
Whoa.

16:45.212 --> 16:49.258
He remembered him because he said he was
ambidextrous and had a really good hook.

16:49.341 --> 16:53.178
According to my father, everyone
expected him to become a world champion,

16:53.262 --> 16:57.683
but he's a piece of shit, I guess,
and he totally ruined it for himself.

16:58.183 --> 16:59.018
Mm.

16:59.101 --> 17:00.853
So then, I asked him some more about it

17:00.936 --> 17:03.772
to see if he might be in touch
with the coach who taught Im Baek-jeong.

17:05.149 --> 17:09.069
I mean a coach is the person who would
know almost anything about his boxer.

17:09.153 --> 17:11.447
Go-to moves, weaknesses, all his steps.

17:11.530 --> 17:14.658
That's right. I bet that you'd know
all of my weaknesses.

17:16.243 --> 17:21.540
I, um, watched the video of you fighting
Im Baek-jeong over and over again.

17:22.291 --> 17:24.585
I was thinking about
what kind of advice I could give you

17:24.668 --> 17:26.837
to help you beat him in a fight, and…

17:30.007 --> 17:33.385
I don't think I'm a good enough coach.
I'm at a loss for answers.

17:34.053 --> 17:35.554
I promise it's not your coaching.

17:35.637 --> 17:38.766
I don't know if I've seen an ambidextrous
fighter that could change up his stance.

17:38.849 --> 17:40.142
I just couldn't keep up with him.

17:41.435 --> 17:43.479
Well, his left jab
looked super strong and heavy.

17:43.562 --> 17:46.231
It was. Also, that right hand's fast.

17:47.483 --> 17:50.360
Honestly, I can't really remember
how I fought.

17:53.947 --> 17:58.786
Yeah, so, Gun-woo, how about
we go and get you trained by that coach?

17:58.869 --> 18:00.704
You know, the one
who taught Im Baek-jeong?

18:01.497 --> 18:02.873
This coach could know

18:03.373 --> 18:05.667
the method that might beat Im Baek-jeong.

18:08.003 --> 18:09.838
-Good idea.
-Is it?

18:10.631 --> 18:11.548
I want to win.

18:15.302 --> 18:16.804
Argh. Ow.

18:16.887 --> 18:18.722
-I'm okay, I'm okay.
-What are you doing?

18:18.806 --> 18:19.890
Huh?

18:20.933 --> 18:22.851
-There's food.
-Oh.

18:35.906 --> 18:37.908
-Eat slowly.
-Hmm.

18:38.450 --> 18:39.284
Here.

18:42.246 --> 18:45.833
I don't want you guys to be
getting into something dangerous.

18:49.920 --> 18:52.214
It just breaks my heart
when you guys get hurt.

18:55.092 --> 18:56.552
Don't worry too much, Mom.

18:56.635 --> 18:59.221
How can I not worry
when you're hurt like that?

19:03.267 --> 19:05.018
I'll take better care of him, Mom.

19:07.563 --> 19:08.605
Go ahead.

19:11.275 --> 19:14.153
-Is there any kimchi?
-Just eat your food.

19:15.112 --> 19:15.988
Mm.

19:16.572 --> 19:19.616
Let's grab those kimchi noodles
from the convenience store afterwards.

19:19.700 --> 19:21.410
-Pretty much the same thing.
-Let's do that.

19:23.453 --> 19:25.664
Damn, this egg tastes better cold.

19:26.915 --> 19:29.209
I used the entire carton of eggs.

19:29.293 --> 19:31.003
Don't eat too fast.

19:31.086 --> 19:32.671
-Hmm.
-Here.

19:34.131 --> 19:37.467
We are currently divided into two teams
that are working in two shifts.

19:37.551 --> 19:42.264
As of now, both Team A and Team B will be
staying on the 16th floor of the hotel.

19:42.347 --> 19:45.350
If we encounter a situation,
both teams can respond together.

19:46.643 --> 19:48.896
So then, how many people is that?

19:48.979 --> 19:50.772
There are a total of 12 personnel.

19:50.856 --> 19:53.025
Uh, you can vouch for their skills?

19:53.108 --> 19:54.401
Yes, you don't have to worry.

19:54.484 --> 19:55.402
Ah.

19:58.280 --> 19:59.615
Uh, when…

20:00.365 --> 20:01.783
When we take down Im Baek-jeong,

20:02.743 --> 20:05.120
will the Major Crimes Unit be enough?

20:09.041 --> 20:10.417
No, not at all.

20:11.460 --> 20:12.878
Should I call the mobile unit?

20:13.670 --> 20:16.215
Uh, that's not what I meant.

20:17.633 --> 20:21.970
We still don't know who took the money
from Im Baek-jeong, and it's worrying.

20:24.932 --> 20:28.143
Mr. Min, would you like me
to get some Marines?

20:31.104 --> 20:32.356
It wouldn't work.

20:32.439 --> 20:34.107
Oh, yeah.

20:35.025 --> 20:36.735
What about the Green Pine Tree Club?

20:41.573 --> 20:42.532
Oh.

20:43.033 --> 20:44.660
Yoon Han-gu, the sergeant?

20:47.412 --> 20:49.915
Is Han-gu in Suwon currently?

20:49.998 --> 20:55.045
Yeah. Baek-jeong's money
shouldn't have gone out that far so…

20:56.338 --> 20:57.965
Okay, I'll reach out to him.

21:07.057 --> 21:08.141
Hey.

21:09.768 --> 21:10.894
Hey, Diego.

21:13.355 --> 21:15.399
You sure know how to pick a place to meet.

21:16.566 --> 21:18.151
Happy birthday, Captain.

21:23.824 --> 21:25.033
I asked for US dollars.

21:25.117 --> 21:27.703
I'm sorry. I didn't have enough time.

21:31.748 --> 21:34.501
I'm gonna need an extra 10%
when we get to Bangkok.

21:39.589 --> 21:41.216
Yeah, fine.

21:41.717 --> 21:43.218
Wednesday, 3 a.m.

21:45.804 --> 21:46.888
See you in Cheongju.

21:47.889 --> 21:49.891
Yeah. Okay.

21:52.394 --> 21:53.395
Understood.

22:00.110 --> 22:01.987
